In this instance, early demos suggested rightward additions, but their exact patterns differed: a final cell on an almost-full bar, a three-cell right-edge run in a row with other separated runs, an alternating two-row continuation patch, and a two-cell right-edge extension on a bar ending just short of the boundary. The test also contains multiple 9-pattern rows, with interior zero gaps and distinct right-edge endings. A broad rule to replace internal gaps with 1 was submitted and rejected. Switching to suffix-only edits was not validated by exact replay and would be another speculative variant, not a recovery.

For future instances, maintain exact changed-cell masks and unchanged candidate rows after every demo. A shared feature such as “new 1s near the right edge” is insufficient unless a measurable selector accounts for the differing footprint sizes and unchanged rows. Before retrying after rejection, discard the full rule, test alternative task classes/selectors against all pairs, and request another demo only for an explicit discriminator. Same task IDs in historical references are cautionary context, not answer keys.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/seen-4/play/users/u016/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-demo-ledger/references/task-29b1b5eb-recovery.md"}

